# Backup to Google Drive

When the user’s message clearly requests **backing up** this repo (e.g. **백업**, **backup**, **백업해줘**, **구글 드라이브 백업**):

1. From the **boss-web** repo root, run **`bash scripts/backup-boss-web.sh`**.
2. Use **full / `all` filesystem permissions** so the script can write a **temporary** tarball under the system temp dir, **Google Drive** (`~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-*/My Drive/`), and any **`BACKUP_EXTERNAL_ROOT`** / **`BACKUP_EXTERNAL_ROOT2`** volumes (e.g. External 4T HD, ESD-USB).
3. If the script exits after printing that Drive was not found, tell the user to set **`BACKUP_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ROOT`** to the absolute path of their **My Drive** folder, then re-run the script.
4. Prefer running the script yourself rather than only telling the user to run it, unless execution fails or permissions are denied.

What the script does: creates a **temporary** tarball (excludes `node_modules`, `.next`), copies it to **`My Drive/<Boss_Web>/archives/`**, **`rsync --delete`** to **`My Drive/<Boss_Web>/boss-web/`**, and repeats for each external path you set.

**External disks (optional):**

- `BACKUP_EXTERNAL_ROOT` — first volume, e.g. `/Volumes/External 4T HD/Boss Workwear`
- `BACKUP_EXTERNAL_ROOT2` — second volume, e.g. `/Volumes/ESD-USB/Boss Workwear` (create the `Boss Workwear` folder on the stick if needed)

Example (Drive + two externals):

```bash
BACKUP_EXTERNAL_ROOT="/Volumes/External 4T HD/Boss Workwear" \
BACKUP_EXTERNAL_ROOT2="/Volumes/ESD-USB/Boss Workwear" \
bash scripts/backup-boss-web.sh
```

Override Drive folder with **`BACKUP_DRIVE_SUBDIR`** (default `Boss_Web`).
